1
00:00:00,610 --> 00:00:01,870
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,640
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:05,410
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:08,410
(Episode 41)

5
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:09,850
You haven't...

6
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:11,750
really changed at all, So Yeon.

7
00:00:13,490 --> 00:00:17,520
When Seong Woo was still alive,
we used to meet up quite often.

8
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:24,260
After all, he was the only friend
I could truly open up to.

9
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:26,600
Seong Woo and I...

10
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,300
were the best of friends.

11
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:32,970
You weren't.

12
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:37,480
I remember everything.

13
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:40,950
On the day my husband died,

14
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:44,580
you were shouting at him.

15
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:47,350
You yelled at him,
saying he just needed...

16
00:00:47,350 --> 00:00:48,690
to shut his mouth.

17
00:00:57,860 --> 00:00:59,860
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

18
00:01:01,370 --> 00:01:04,000
Hae Ra isn't used
to doing things like this,

19
00:01:04,070 --> 00:01:05,640
so I think she was a little nervous.

20
00:01:05,770 --> 00:01:06,870
Are you badly hurt?

21
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:09,470
No, it's just a small cut.

22
00:01:09,710 --> 00:01:12,010
You should always be careful
with knives.

23
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:16,580
So Yeon, try some of this fruit.

24
00:01:16,650 --> 00:01:18,380
It's very sweet and delicious.

25
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:20,290
Thank you.

26
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:25,120
Here.

27
00:01:35,230 --> 00:01:36,840
(Traffic Accident
Criminal Settlement Agreement)

28
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:40,440
I remember everything.

29
00:01:42,410 --> 00:01:44,940
On the day my husband died,

30
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:48,680
you were shouting at him.

31
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:51,380
You yelled at him,
saying he just needed...

32
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:52,580
to shut his mouth.

33
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,600
The Chairman said that from now on,

34
00:02:08,770 --> 00:02:10,570
I should serve you warm tea
instead of hard liquor.

35
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:11,640
Okay.

36
00:02:12,470 --> 00:02:13,770
Where did she go?

37
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:16,370
She went shopping
with So Yeon and the others.

38
00:02:17,180 --> 00:02:20,580
Unbelievable.
I told her to keep her distance.

39
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:26,920
Get some rest, then.

40
00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:29,790
Right, thank you.

41
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:45,300
Kang Young Hoon...

42
00:02:46,070 --> 00:02:49,170
is definitely hiding something.

43
00:03:23,410 --> 00:03:26,080
A criminal settlement
for a traffic accident?

44
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:39,520
(Victim: Cha Seong Woo (Deceased),
Son: Cha Seok Jin)

45
00:03:40,730 --> 00:03:42,830
The victim is Cha Seong Woo?

46
00:03:44,930 --> 00:03:47,130
Chief Cha's father?

47
00:03:50,570 --> 00:03:53,340
Why does CEO Kang have
the settlement agreement...

48
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:55,640
for Chief Cha's father's accident?

49
00:04:00,450 --> 00:04:02,580
(Traffic Accident
Criminal Settlement Agreement)

50
00:04:02,650 --> 00:04:04,380
The perpetrator is Oh Tae Seop.

51
00:04:07,890 --> 00:04:09,050
Oh Tae Seop?

52
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:12,590
That name sounds very familiar.

53
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:16,660
(Cheongma)

54
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:21,570
You found this
on Team Leader Seo's laptop?

55
00:04:22,330 --> 00:04:24,240
Yes. Just as you instructed,

56
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:27,070
I pretended to drop off a gift
and sneaked in.

57
00:04:28,770 --> 00:04:31,540
He has been gathering
quite the collection.

58
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:35,880
So this is how he's been
digging into me behind my back?

59
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:38,480
I have to admire his effort.

60
00:04:38,950 --> 00:04:40,020
What should we do?

61
00:04:40,590 --> 00:04:42,090
Don't make a move just yet.

62
00:04:42,950 --> 00:04:44,390
I've already warned him,

63
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:46,860
so he won't be able to do
anything drastic for now.

64
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:48,760
Understood.

65
00:04:49,830 --> 00:04:52,000
This is the company master key.

66
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,530
Keep a close eye on Team Leader Seo.

67
00:04:56,130 --> 00:04:58,040
But lay low for the time being.

68
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:01,410
Right now, he's probably
keeping tabs on our movements.

69
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:05,510
And I've also secured
the personal information...

70
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:07,410
of the detective who helped him.

71
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:08,680
Good job.

72
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:12,120
That jerk of a detective
will also be crucial later,

73
00:05:12,850 --> 00:05:13,920
so keep a close watch on him.

74
00:05:14,850 --> 00:05:16,250
Yes, understood.

75
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:22,790
Hey, Teun Teun's having
a family sports day.

76
00:05:23,830 --> 00:05:25,600
He's not even in school yet,

77
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:27,970
so why are there
so many family functions?

78
00:05:29,570 --> 00:05:31,800
The highlight of fall is sports day.

79
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:35,510
You eat gimbap and run a marathon.

80
00:05:36,610 --> 00:05:38,510
It's not always a good thing.

81
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:40,080
Why not?

82
00:05:41,650 --> 00:05:43,380
Boss, you must be awful at running.

83
00:05:44,250 --> 00:05:45,920
Don't tell me
you'll come in dead last.

84
00:05:46,980 --> 00:05:48,350
I need to go watch to see...

85
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:50,090
what place you come in.

86
00:05:51,690 --> 00:05:53,190
I'm not going.

87
00:05:55,490 --> 00:05:57,930
- Why not?
- I have to open the cafe.

88
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:00,870
You should take a day off
for an event like that.

89
00:06:00,970 --> 00:06:02,970
Imagine how disappointed
Teun Teun will be.

90
00:06:03,330 --> 00:06:05,270
Teun Teun doesn't have to go either.

91
00:06:05,340 --> 00:06:06,900
It's not mandatory like school.

92
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:10,310
Is it because
you have no one to go with?

93
00:06:11,180 --> 00:06:13,580
Hyun Jae's away on a business trip,

94
00:06:14,050 --> 00:06:15,650
but I wasn't planning
on going anyway.

95
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:18,220
You should go...

96
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:19,480
with me.

97
00:06:20,950 --> 00:06:23,190
Teun Teun has more than one uncle,

98
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:24,760
so I can go instead.

99
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:28,390
Look, it says right here.

100
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,900
Any family member can participate.

101
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:34,500
I'm practically family anyway.

102
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,070
Forget it.

103
00:06:36,170 --> 00:06:38,870
If you go
and your grandmother finds out,

104
00:06:39,270 --> 00:06:40,440
she'll throw a fit.

105
00:06:40,710 --> 00:06:41,870
Just the thought of it
makes me shiver.

106
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:44,510
Come on.
Why are you overthinking it?

107
00:06:44,940 --> 00:06:47,550
Just think about having
a fun day with Teun Teun.

108
00:06:48,310 --> 00:06:50,410
Anyway, I'll be at the event.

109
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:53,320
Just make sure the gimbap
is extra delicious.

110
00:06:56,450 --> 00:06:59,490
Sweet, there's a marathon for dads.

111
00:07:00,990 --> 00:07:03,230
Wait, there's also
a three-legged race.

112
00:07:05,060 --> 00:07:07,900
Check out the grand prize.
It's an oven.

113
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:10,230
I don't have one at home.

114
00:07:10,770 --> 00:07:13,740
Boss, we've got
to win first place, okay?

115
00:07:13,810 --> 00:07:16,570
You think winning is that easy?
Unbelievable.

116
00:07:22,910 --> 00:07:25,580
Mom, I bet you've been
feeling down lately.

117
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:28,250
The board rejected
that scholarship program,

118
00:07:28,550 --> 00:07:30,890
and it was the first one
you designed.

119
00:07:31,190 --> 00:07:33,660
You sure took
your sweet time asking.

120
00:07:35,130 --> 00:07:36,830
Of course I was upset.

121
00:07:37,330 --> 00:07:40,430
However, I can use this opportunity
to fix what was lacking...

122
00:07:40,830 --> 00:07:43,500
and resubmit it
at the next board meeting.

123
00:07:44,770 --> 00:07:46,340
I need to treat this failure
as a lesson...

124
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:47,770
and try once more.

125
00:07:48,510 --> 00:07:50,810
Mom, you're inspiring as always.

126
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:53,440
Anyway, that got me thinking.

127
00:07:54,450 --> 00:07:57,010
Should I try coming up
with a scholarship program too?

128
00:07:57,380 --> 00:07:59,780
It's time I start learning
the foundation's work too.

129
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:02,790
She's right about that.

130
00:08:02,950 --> 00:08:04,920
Having Hae Ra support you...

131
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,490
and learn
about the foundation's work...

132
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:08,030
would give you
a lot more reassurance.

133
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:13,930
That's true, but...

134
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,240
It feels a bit premature.

135
00:08:18,770 --> 00:08:20,140
To be honest,

136
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:22,270
I haven't fully established
my own footing...

137
00:08:22,270 --> 00:08:23,370
at the foundation yet.

138
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:26,310
Even the scholarship program
I'm pushing for...

139
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:28,010
hasn't been approved yet.

140
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:30,350
If Hae Ra steps in
to learn the ropes now,

141
00:08:30,410 --> 00:08:32,050
what would people say?

142
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:35,120
But she needs to start now...

143
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:38,020
so she can get a feel for
how the foundation operates.

144
00:08:38,490 --> 00:08:41,430
She's also very keen
to learn the job.

145
00:08:42,290 --> 00:08:45,660
Eagerness alone isn't enough
to handle the work.

146
00:08:47,270 --> 00:08:50,770
Honestly, I don't think Hae Ra
has really proven herself yet...

147
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:53,800
as the design team lead.

148
00:08:54,270 --> 00:08:57,170
Not true. Haven't you seen
that Shoejoy's sales went up?

149
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:59,680
The response to the new product
is amazing.

150
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:02,750
You didn't achieve that
entirely on your own.

151
00:09:02,950 --> 00:09:05,180
Above all, you need
to earn recognition for your work...

152
00:09:05,220 --> 00:09:07,180
in your current role first.

153
00:09:07,550 --> 00:09:10,350
That way, when you learn the work
at the foundation later,

154
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:12,920
people won't talk behind your back.

155
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:24,500
I can't believe my mom.

156
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:27,670
Why won't she let me do
what even Ko Eun Seol gets to do?

157
00:09:28,510 --> 00:09:30,440
Because you're different
from Ko Eun Seol.

158
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:33,340
You're the one
who will reach the top.

159
00:09:33,410 --> 00:09:36,650
Still, isn't she giving me
way too little credit?

160
00:09:36,780 --> 00:09:38,750
I'm more than capable
of doing a great job.

161
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:40,790
Just like the Chairman said,

162
00:09:40,850 --> 00:09:43,520
show some results
as head of the design team first.

163
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:45,720
She has a point, you know.

164
00:09:49,890 --> 00:09:51,030
By the way, Ms. Joo,

165
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,500
I've been wondering for a while.

166
00:09:54,730 --> 00:09:56,770
Why are you supporting me this much?

167
00:09:58,340 --> 00:09:59,340
What?

168
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:00,570
I mean, it's true.

169
00:10:01,110 --> 00:10:03,910
You care for me more
than my own parents,

170
00:10:04,580 --> 00:10:05,980
which got me wondering.

171
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:09,180
Well, that's...

172
00:10:09,850 --> 00:10:11,650
I'm supporting you
for Cheongma's sake.

173
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:15,020
For Cheongma?

174
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:16,490
Yes, of course.

175
00:10:16,690 --> 00:10:20,120
I believe what's best for you
is what's best for Cheongma.

176
00:10:20,690 --> 00:10:23,130
Cheongma is the company
founded by the former chairman.

177
00:10:23,190 --> 00:10:25,930
Having you, his granddaughter,
inherit it...

178
00:10:26,330 --> 00:10:27,930
is the ideal scenario.

179
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:29,930
That makes sense.

180
00:10:30,570 --> 00:10:33,770
Your affection for me is really
your affection for Cheongma.

181
00:10:35,470 --> 00:10:36,470
That's right.

182
00:10:37,310 --> 00:10:40,440
But why don't my parents see
what's so obvious to you?

183
00:10:40,510 --> 00:10:42,010
It's so frustrating.

184
00:10:42,150 --> 00:10:45,480
That's why you have to prove
you're a reliable daughter.

185
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:47,620
I understand.

186
00:10:47,790 --> 00:10:50,190
I'll work hard
and prove my worth to them.

187
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:52,060
I'll get going then.

188
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:09,610
(Traffic Accident
Criminal Settlement Agreement)

189
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:22,220
It's me. I need you to find someone.

190
00:11:22,950 --> 00:11:26,560
I'll send you a photo,
so look into the perpetrator in it.

191
00:11:27,660 --> 00:11:28,690
Oh Tae Seop.

192
00:11:29,130 --> 00:11:31,930
Find out everything you can
about him.

193
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:35,230
I think Director Jung
and Director Hwang...

194
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:36,970
are the most stubborn.

195
00:11:37,540 --> 00:11:40,770
- I know.
- They're highly conservative,

196
00:11:41,070 --> 00:11:43,610
and they seem to care the most about
what the CEO thinks.

197
00:11:43,870 --> 00:11:45,880
I see you've got them
all figured out.

198
00:11:47,380 --> 00:11:49,510
I catch on pretty fast.

199
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:52,850
I have well over 20 years of experience
reading the room.

200
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:56,520
The corporate image
is just an excuse.

201
00:11:57,120 --> 00:11:58,790
Ultimately, they don't want
to get on the CEO's bad side,

202
00:11:58,860 --> 00:12:01,430
so they'll surely vote against it
at the next board meeting.

203
00:12:01,490 --> 00:12:02,960
You're probably right.

204
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:06,560
Is there any other way to sway them?

205
00:12:07,470 --> 00:12:10,430
If we can't convince them,
we need to give them a valid reason.

206
00:12:11,170 --> 00:12:12,740
One they can't oppose.

207
00:12:14,470 --> 00:12:15,510
What reason would that be?

208
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:21,850
If the CEO comes over to our side,
they'll naturally follow.

209
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:26,550
It won't be easy
to convince the CEO.

210
00:12:27,450 --> 00:12:30,120
On the surface,
he appears to support the Chairman,

211
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:33,460
but everyone knows
they're secretly in competition.

212
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:38,130
That's the only way to pass
the scholarship program.

213
00:12:38,630 --> 00:12:40,300
You look so sure of yourself.

214
00:12:40,870 --> 00:12:43,070
Do you have some special plan...

215
00:12:44,030 --> 00:12:45,670
to win the CEO over?

216
00:12:57,650 --> 00:12:59,620
Ms. Kang, I don't think
I've seen that purse before.

217
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:00,950
Is it new?

218
00:13:01,890 --> 00:13:02,890
This?

219
00:13:03,350 --> 00:13:06,060
I went shopping with Chief Cha's mother
over the weekend.

220
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:08,130
He bought it for me.

221
00:13:08,230 --> 00:13:10,430
I think
it suits your vibe perfectly.

222
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:12,300
Well, in my case,

223
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:14,130
there's nothing
that doesn't look good on me.

224
00:13:16,070 --> 00:13:20,500
By the way, I think the Chief and I
are going to set a wedding date.

225
00:13:20,870 --> 00:13:22,010
Really?

226
00:13:22,610 --> 00:13:25,110
We had dinner with both
of our parents this past weekend.

227
00:13:25,810 --> 00:13:27,580
Then are you getting married
this year?

228
00:13:27,650 --> 00:13:29,050
I suppose so.

229
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:30,480
That reminds me.

230
00:13:30,550 --> 00:13:33,380
I don't plan on accepting
wedding gift money.

231
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:35,790
What would I do
with your pocket change?

232
00:13:37,690 --> 00:13:39,220
So I'm letting you know in advance,

233
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:40,360
there's no pressure
to bring anything.

234
00:13:40,890 --> 00:13:41,890
- Sure.
- Got it.

235
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:45,030
Ko Eun Seol, you're invited too.

236
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:46,800
Wait.

237
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,330
Will it be too awkward for you?

238
00:13:50,430 --> 00:13:52,600
No, I'll be there.

239
00:13:53,540 --> 00:13:55,040
I'll be there to congratulate you...

240
00:13:55,770 --> 00:13:57,410
and eat my fill of free food.

241
00:13:58,610 --> 00:13:59,640
Suit yourself.

242
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:02,450
I just hope
you don't get indigestion.

243
00:14:09,090 --> 00:14:13,560
By the way, I think the Chief and I
are going to set a wedding date.

244
00:14:34,650 --> 00:14:35,650
Come in.

245
00:14:39,180 --> 00:14:40,750
I hope I'm not interrupting.

246
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,520
Not at all. Please have a seat.

247
00:14:48,530 --> 00:14:51,200
Did you have a good time shopping
with your mother the other day?

248
00:14:51,260 --> 00:14:53,730
Yes. My mother
really enjoyed it too.

249
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:55,300
I'm glad to hear that.

250
00:14:56,300 --> 00:14:59,240
But from what I saw,

251
00:14:59,270 --> 00:15:02,070
she seemed a bit uncomfortable
during the meal.

252
00:15:03,910 --> 00:15:06,510
She usually feels uncomfortable
in unfamiliar settings.

253
00:15:07,750 --> 00:15:08,850
I see.

254
00:15:11,250 --> 00:15:13,920
I feel a little awkward asking,

255
00:15:15,250 --> 00:15:17,790
but how's your mother doing
these days?

256
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:19,760
If I know how she's doing,

257
00:15:20,090 --> 00:15:22,490
I might be able to help out
in some way.

258
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:24,130
My mother...

259
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,500
lost her memory from the shock
of my father's accident.

260
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:30,870
Along with the trauma,
she suffered a mental regression.

261
00:15:31,970 --> 00:15:34,170
She has the mental capacity
of a child under ten,

262
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:37,940
but sometimes
her memory comes back briefly.

263
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:41,080
Oh, I see.

264
00:15:42,180 --> 00:15:44,880
I knew that your mother was unwell,

265
00:15:45,050 --> 00:15:47,950
but this is the first time
I'm hearing it directly from you.

266
00:15:49,450 --> 00:15:51,790
Let me know if there's anything
I can do to help in the future.

267
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:53,990
Thank you, Ms. Joo.

268
00:15:57,390 --> 00:16:00,200
What if
that woman's memory comes back?

269
00:16:01,330 --> 00:16:04,700
Even if I keep a close eye on her,
I still feel anxious.

270
00:16:05,970 --> 00:16:08,470
I need something more certain.

271
00:16:09,270 --> 00:16:12,780
Something that will reassure
Chief Cha and that woman.

272
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:21,350
- Did you call for me, sir?
- Yes.

273
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:23,120
Have a seat.

274
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:24,460
Yes, sir.

275
00:16:27,790 --> 00:16:29,760
Did you get home safely
the other day?

276
00:16:30,190 --> 00:16:31,200
Yes.

277
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:33,460
My mother was very pleased
with the shopping, too.

278
00:16:33,930 --> 00:16:35,030
I'm glad to hear that.

279
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:38,600
The reason I called you here...

280
00:16:40,570 --> 00:16:43,970
is because I was hoping you
and Hae Ra would get engaged.

281
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:46,680
An engagement?

282
00:16:47,540 --> 00:16:50,510
Well, getting married seems
a bit premature right now.

283
00:16:51,580 --> 00:16:52,780
And above all,

284
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:55,720
you just launched your brand,

285
00:16:56,090 --> 00:16:59,260
so wouldn't it be a shame if it got
overshadowed by marriage news?

286
00:16:59,790 --> 00:17:00,790
Since Hae Ra's...

287
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:03,260
in such a rush to get married,

288
00:17:03,660 --> 00:17:07,260
having an engagement ceremony
might calm her down a bit.

289
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:11,400
What do you think?

290
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:14,770
That sounds good to me too.

291
00:17:18,110 --> 00:17:19,380
Are you sure about that?

292
00:17:20,510 --> 00:17:22,010
You don't seem
very certain about it.

293
00:17:22,010 --> 00:17:24,680
I am. It just feels
a little sudden, that's all.

294
00:17:26,750 --> 00:17:28,420
I'll get engaged to Hae Ra.

295
00:17:29,420 --> 00:17:30,850
Yes, good.

296
00:17:31,490 --> 00:17:33,190
Let's make
your relationship official...

297
00:17:33,190 --> 00:17:34,320
with an engagement first.

298
00:17:35,030 --> 00:17:38,600
Since there are so many rumors
going around about you two,

299
00:17:39,230 --> 00:17:41,100
using this opportunity
to make things clear...

300
00:17:41,130 --> 00:17:42,530
wouldn't be a bad idea.

301
00:17:43,430 --> 00:17:44,470
Yes, sir.

302
00:17:50,110 --> 00:17:51,110
Seok Jin!

303
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:54,950
Let me breathe, will you?

304
00:17:55,810 --> 00:17:58,120
What's going on?
What's gotten into Dad?

305
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:02,420
It seems like he totally made up
his mind after that dinner. Nice.

306
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:04,250
If he was going
to agree this easily,

307
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:05,620
why did he make such a fuss before?

308
00:18:06,060 --> 00:18:07,120
It's an engagement, not a wedding.

309
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:09,130
We're just promising to get married,
that's all.

310
00:18:09,660 --> 00:18:11,260
Nothing's really going to change.

311
00:18:11,660 --> 00:18:12,860
How is it the same?

312
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:16,070
It makes it official
that we're taken.

313
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:17,630
It's no different from a wedding.

314
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:19,800
There you go,
getting ahead of yourself again.

315
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:22,510
It's just our families
getting together to have a meal.

316
00:18:23,070 --> 00:18:25,740
That's how normal people do it,
but we're different.

317
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:27,780
Trust me, it's the exact same thing.

318
00:18:28,450 --> 00:18:29,980
Don't make such a big fuss about it.

319
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:32,780
No way. I want a grand ceremony.

320
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:34,220
Even grander than a typical wedding.

321
00:18:34,820 --> 00:18:36,890
We're getting new rings too, right?

322
00:18:37,450 --> 00:18:39,460
This time,
I really want something flashy.

323
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:40,960
Unbelievable.

324
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:43,330
Forget it.
Just wear the one you have.

325
00:18:46,730 --> 00:18:48,770
- Sir.
- You're here.

326
00:18:49,770 --> 00:18:51,000
Here you go.

327
00:18:55,670 --> 00:18:57,270
This really wasn't necessary.

328
00:18:57,610 --> 00:18:59,810
I already confirmed the deposit
from last time.

329
00:19:00,010 --> 00:19:02,350
It's no big deal.
Please keep taking good care...

330
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:04,080
of our old man.

331
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:06,580
Don't you worry about that.

332
00:19:06,750 --> 00:19:10,090
Lately, he has just been
cooped up in his room.

333
00:19:20,930 --> 00:19:22,730
Looks like you stayed
tucked away all day.

334
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,040
That's right.
Let's keep it this way.

335
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:27,910
It's easier for both of us.

336
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:30,570
Tell me about it.

337
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:33,710
Lately, I haven't been leaving
this room at all.

338
00:19:34,110 --> 00:19:35,480
Yes, that's good to hear.

339
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:37,310
By the way,

340
00:19:37,610 --> 00:19:39,750
have you been staying away
from the gambling arcades too?

341
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:41,920
What?

342
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:47,960
I only go once in a while.
I just play for a little bit.

343
00:19:48,730 --> 00:19:50,290
Is that so?

344
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:56,130
I picked up some snacks,
so grab one when you get bored.

345
00:19:57,730 --> 00:20:00,670
Mr. Choi, you really
are the best, as always.

346
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:02,570
Thanks, I'll enjoy them.

347
00:20:02,570 --> 00:20:04,940
Then, I'll see you here tomorrow.

348
00:20:06,110 --> 00:20:07,640
Make sure you're here.

349
00:20:08,410 --> 00:20:11,320
Right, of course. See you tomorrow.

350
00:20:14,050 --> 00:20:15,090
Take care.

351
00:20:30,870 --> 00:20:32,040
Joo Ae Sook.

352
00:20:34,140 --> 00:20:35,910
I'm finding our daughter
no matter what.

353
00:20:36,510 --> 00:20:39,080
She must be alive somewhere.

354
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:42,850
Otherwise, what are you so afraid of
that you send him over every day?

355
00:20:43,980 --> 00:20:46,650
If I turn up with our daughter,

356
00:20:48,350 --> 00:20:49,920
you won't be able to do
a thing about it.

357
00:20:51,050 --> 00:20:52,060
Just you wait.

358
00:20:52,860 --> 00:20:54,930
You'll be on your knees
in front of your husband...

359
00:20:55,760 --> 00:20:58,260
begging for forgiveness
just like before.

360
00:21:00,560 --> 00:21:02,000
You want to do an interview?

361
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:03,800
Yes.

362
00:21:04,100 --> 00:21:06,200
Even if
it's for the scholarship program,

363
00:21:07,040 --> 00:21:10,640
revealing your past like that
could be dangerous.

364
00:21:11,210 --> 00:21:12,510
If it isn't just an article,

365
00:21:12,780 --> 00:21:14,510
but an interview you give yourself,

366
00:21:15,050 --> 00:21:16,810
everyone will recognize you.

367
00:21:17,010 --> 00:21:19,480
It has to be that extreme
to actually make an impact.

368
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:22,850
The world needs to know
the importance...

369
00:21:22,920 --> 00:21:24,420
of the scholarship program...

370
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:26,560
our foundation
is trying to establish.

371
00:21:28,090 --> 00:21:30,390
Doing this will draw
a lot of attention,

372
00:21:30,630 --> 00:21:32,760
ensuring the scholarship program
gets approved.

373
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:34,700
But still,

374
00:21:35,030 --> 00:21:37,730
your retrial
hasn't even started yet.

375
00:21:38,140 --> 00:21:39,200
Are you sure you'll be okay?

376
00:21:39,500 --> 00:21:42,370
I'm not going to hide anymore.

377
00:21:43,370 --> 00:21:46,910
I have to stand tall
for people to believe me.

378
00:21:49,450 --> 00:21:51,050
If you're really set on this,

379
00:21:51,380 --> 00:21:53,150
I'll look into a place
for the interview.

380
00:21:54,080 --> 00:21:56,520
I knew it.
You're the best, Attorney Seo.

381
00:21:57,290 --> 00:22:00,120
Don't worry too much.
You know how tough I am.

382
00:22:01,460 --> 00:22:04,960
I know all too well.
That's why you should go easy.

383
00:22:05,500 --> 00:22:06,830
Gosh, I'm hungry.

384
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:08,500
Should we grab dinner
before heading home?

385
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:10,230
Sure, sounds good.

386
00:22:13,240 --> 00:22:15,470
- I'm home.
- Hey, you're back.

387
00:22:15,810 --> 00:22:17,870
You're home later than usual.
Have you had dinner?

388
00:22:18,080 --> 00:22:20,510
I ate with Attorney Seo
on my way home.

389
00:22:20,710 --> 00:22:22,680
- I'll go change my clothes.
- Okay, sure.

390
00:22:26,180 --> 00:22:27,250
Attorney Seo?

391
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:29,590
The landlady's younger brother.

392
00:22:29,650 --> 00:22:32,390
Wait, is Eun Seol dating him?

393
00:22:32,390 --> 00:22:34,120
I thought so too,

394
00:22:34,460 --> 00:22:35,530
but I guess not.

395
00:22:36,190 --> 00:22:39,630
They both jumped up and down
denying that they're together.

396
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:41,930
And you believe that?

397
00:22:42,630 --> 00:22:45,240
When a grown man and woman
hang out late at night,

398
00:22:45,570 --> 00:22:48,110
it means they have feelings
for each other.

399
00:22:48,410 --> 00:22:49,870
I'm telling you, they aren't dating.

400
00:22:49,940 --> 00:22:51,580
I can tell just by looking
into Eun Seol's eyes.

401
00:22:51,640 --> 00:22:52,910
They're definitely not dating.

402
00:22:53,040 --> 00:22:55,750
As if you'd know.

403
00:22:55,910 --> 00:22:59,050
As her father, you should be trying
to set them up somehow.

404
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:02,120
Think about it.
Who else can Eun Seol date?

405
00:23:02,750 --> 00:23:06,720
She spent ten years in prison.
Who would even date her now?

406
00:23:06,890 --> 00:23:09,690
There you go again. She'll hear you.

407
00:23:09,760 --> 00:23:11,960
What kind of man
would want to marry her?

408
00:23:13,130 --> 00:23:15,030
Her best bet
is the young man next door...

409
00:23:15,030 --> 00:23:16,530
who knows her whole situation.

410
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:24,640
So you need to step up
and try to talk them into it.

411
00:23:25,710 --> 00:23:27,440
Wait. Should I?

412
00:23:28,180 --> 00:23:29,380
You're unbelievable.

413
00:23:36,090 --> 00:23:37,090
Grandma.

414
00:23:37,950 --> 00:23:38,960
Yes?

415
00:23:39,020 --> 00:23:40,360
I'm not going to get married.

416
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:41,790
You won't get married?

417
00:23:43,030 --> 00:23:44,460
Did you hear everything?

418
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:48,300
Mom, did you swallow a megaphone?
How could she not hear that?

419
00:23:48,370 --> 00:23:50,270
It's not like
Eun Seol wears hearing aids.

420
00:23:51,570 --> 00:23:53,400
I'm never getting married.

421
00:23:53,470 --> 00:23:56,370
I'm just going to stay
with you and Dad forever.

422
00:23:56,840 --> 00:24:00,010
So don't worry about me
not having a man in my life.

423
00:24:00,010 --> 00:24:01,780
How can I not worry?

424
00:24:02,450 --> 00:24:04,380
Even if he's a bit lacking
like your dad,

425
00:24:04,780 --> 00:24:07,580
you need a man to take care of you.

426
00:24:07,650 --> 00:24:09,620
Why are you dragging me into this?

427
00:24:10,420 --> 00:24:14,830
I don't need a man.
I have you and Dad, don't I?

428
00:24:15,830 --> 00:24:16,930
Exactly. Never get married.

429
00:24:17,730 --> 00:24:20,730
Our Eun Seol lacks nothing, so why
would she go chasing after a man?

430
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:22,670
Men should be lining up
for her instead.

431
00:24:23,130 --> 00:24:24,700
So don't get married.

432
00:24:25,070 --> 00:24:27,270
Just live with me
for the rest of your life.

433
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:28,940
Okay, sounds good.

434
00:24:29,310 --> 00:24:32,840
- Perfect.
- This sure is terrifying.

435
00:24:33,440 --> 00:24:38,080
The two of you are so alike,
it's almost scary.

436
00:24:38,380 --> 00:24:41,480
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

437
00:24:48,490 --> 00:24:50,090
Director Joo, what brings you here?

438
00:24:51,360 --> 00:24:52,730
Nothing much.

439
00:24:53,100 --> 00:24:54,870
I just wanted to see
if you got my gift.

440
00:24:55,100 --> 00:24:58,540
Right, I was actually planning
to return it to you.

441
00:25:05,580 --> 00:25:08,010
I see no reason
for me to accept this.

442
00:25:08,610 --> 00:25:11,310
So you're just going to return it?

443
00:25:13,050 --> 00:25:14,680
It's right there
in the note I wrote.

444
00:25:15,720 --> 00:25:18,390
I'm thanking you
for helping Eun Seol.

445
00:25:18,660 --> 00:25:21,320
My helping her has nothing to do
with the company.

446
00:25:22,190 --> 00:25:24,690
Besides, helping her
is a personal matter for me.

447
00:25:26,430 --> 00:25:29,300
I don't think it's something
you need to thank me for.

448
00:25:32,240 --> 00:25:36,240
Whenever I meet someone
as self-righteous as you, Mr. Seo,

449
00:25:36,570 --> 00:25:37,840
I find it quite amusing.

450
00:25:38,910 --> 00:25:40,910
It just makes me want to break them.

451
00:25:44,750 --> 00:25:47,720
Sure. If you don't want the gift,
I can't force you.

452
00:25:49,290 --> 00:25:50,550
Take care, then.

453
00:25:51,620 --> 00:25:52,620
Wait.

454
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:53,920
By the way,

455
00:25:54,790 --> 00:25:56,790
you said you wanted
to help Eun Seol, right?

456
00:25:58,330 --> 00:25:59,760
That's right. What about it?

457
00:26:00,930 --> 00:26:03,870
Then you shouldn't confuse her.

458
00:26:05,070 --> 00:26:06,500
Her life's been chaotic enough,

459
00:26:06,570 --> 00:26:08,610
and she finally seems
to have found some peace.

460
00:26:09,540 --> 00:26:12,180
I don't know why everyone around her
keeps stirring things up.

461
00:26:13,840 --> 00:26:15,250
I'm not stirring things up.

462
00:26:15,780 --> 00:26:18,210
I'm simply guiding her
in the right direction.

463
00:26:18,950 --> 00:26:20,950
That's just what you think.

464
00:26:22,450 --> 00:26:23,720
I'll leave you to it, then.

465
00:26:40,340 --> 00:26:42,870
Who does he think he is,
stepping out of line like that?

466
00:26:44,110 --> 00:26:46,080
Don't push your luck, Seo Hyun Jae,

467
00:26:46,380 --> 00:26:48,040
or I might just snap you in half.

468
00:26:54,520 --> 00:26:55,590
Come in.

469
00:27:01,490 --> 00:27:03,330
What are you doing here
at this hour?

470
00:27:04,030 --> 00:27:06,800
Do I need a reason to come see you?

471
00:27:10,370 --> 00:27:11,870
So, what's that?

472
00:27:13,800 --> 00:27:17,070
I've been so caught up
in the scholarship foundation...

473
00:27:17,740 --> 00:27:19,910
that I feel like I've neglected you.

474
00:27:20,740 --> 00:27:22,750
Well, you kind of have.

475
00:27:24,010 --> 00:27:27,720
I'm going to take better care
of your health from now on.

476
00:27:28,220 --> 00:27:30,190
You need to manage your blood sugar.

477
00:27:30,590 --> 00:27:32,190
It's best to take this after meals.

478
00:27:32,260 --> 00:27:33,260
- Try one now.
- Okay.

479
00:27:34,260 --> 00:27:35,260
Here.

480
00:27:36,260 --> 00:27:37,260
Thanks.

481
00:27:40,060 --> 00:27:44,930
I know Director Joo
has been taking good care of you.

482
00:27:45,470 --> 00:27:48,000
From now on,
I'll be doing that myself.

483
00:27:48,770 --> 00:27:51,780
Oh, right. I'd appreciate that.

484
00:27:52,340 --> 00:27:54,510
Anyway, Hae Ra told me...

485
00:27:55,380 --> 00:27:57,850
you're letting her get engaged
to Chief Cha.

486
00:27:58,110 --> 00:28:02,050
Yes. Well, I'd like that,
but what do you think?

487
00:28:02,220 --> 00:28:04,350
I think it's a great idea.

488
00:28:04,490 --> 00:28:09,390
I was actually going to suggest
that we let them get engaged first.

489
00:28:11,190 --> 00:28:13,860
Marriage right away
feels a bit much,

490
00:28:14,800 --> 00:28:18,870
but I want to keep Seok Jin close
and see how he does.

491
00:28:19,170 --> 00:28:21,670
Is there really anything left
to wait and see?

492
00:28:23,210 --> 00:28:26,910
It sure takes a lot to become
Kang Young Hoon's son-in-law.

493
00:28:29,280 --> 00:28:31,780
Did you think it'd be easy?

494
00:28:36,320 --> 00:28:39,720
I was hoping you and Hae Ra
would get engaged.

495
00:28:42,230 --> 00:28:43,230
Come in.

496
00:28:48,360 --> 00:28:50,570
Here's the design draft printout
for next season.

497
00:28:50,630 --> 00:28:51,900
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

498
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:53,070
Right, good work.

499
00:28:57,310 --> 00:28:58,310
Is this...

500
00:28:59,440 --> 00:29:00,480
how it's going to be?

501
00:29:00,980 --> 00:29:01,980
Excuse me?

502
00:29:02,750 --> 00:29:04,650
You're acting like you're mad at me.

503
00:29:05,050 --> 00:29:06,250
What do you mean?

504
00:29:07,220 --> 00:29:09,550
I'm being respectful
since you're my superior.

505
00:29:10,390 --> 00:29:12,220
You call this
treating me with respect?

506
00:29:12,390 --> 00:29:14,860
Then is smiling and joking around
like before...

507
00:29:15,560 --> 00:29:17,360
treating you with respect?

508
00:29:17,890 --> 00:29:19,460
That's not what I mean.

509
00:29:19,860 --> 00:29:21,400
You seem to have it wrong,

510
00:29:21,870 --> 00:29:24,530
but you're no longer
my school friend.

511
00:29:25,370 --> 00:29:26,740
That's how I've decided to see it.

512
00:29:27,540 --> 00:29:29,370
- Ko Eun Seol.
- I will be...

513
00:29:29,710 --> 00:29:31,570
even more respectful from now on.

514
00:29:32,540 --> 00:29:33,540
Then...

515
00:29:45,120 --> 00:29:47,420
Now, we'll walk on one and two.

516
00:29:47,560 --> 00:29:48,560
You can do it, right?

517
00:29:48,890 --> 00:29:51,430
- Yes, I can do it.
- Okay, here we go.

518
00:29:51,490 --> 00:29:53,930
- Okay.
- We'll go around that way.

519
00:29:57,930 --> 00:30:01,770
Come on, let go.
That's not necessary.

520
00:30:03,010 --> 00:30:04,570
How else are we supposed
to coordinate our moves?

521
00:30:05,010 --> 00:30:08,310
In a three-legged race,
we need to move as one.

522
00:30:09,310 --> 00:30:11,610
What if your grandmother sees us?

523
00:30:17,490 --> 00:30:18,490
Don't worry.

524
00:30:19,390 --> 00:30:21,490
Okay, from the top.

525
00:30:22,460 --> 00:30:24,960
Off we go. One, two.

526
00:30:26,360 --> 00:30:27,960
Are you a robot, boss?

527
00:30:28,030 --> 00:30:30,330
- How do I do it?
- Like this?

528
00:30:30,330 --> 00:30:32,540
- Left foot first. One, two.
- One, two.

529
00:30:32,570 --> 00:30:34,500
One, two, one.

530
00:30:34,570 --> 00:30:38,240
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

531
00:30:41,280 --> 00:30:43,010
Yes, this is Joo Mi Ran.

532
00:30:43,480 --> 00:30:44,480
Ms. Joo.

533
00:30:44,910 --> 00:30:47,180
It's about the person
you asked me to look into.

534
00:30:48,220 --> 00:30:49,220
Right.

535
00:30:49,390 --> 00:30:51,490
The perpetrator of the accident,
Oh Tae Seop,

536
00:30:53,190 --> 00:30:56,460
turns out to have quite a history.

537
00:30:58,190 --> 00:30:59,600
Who is he?

538
00:31:00,030 --> 00:31:02,130
I see you didn't know.

539
00:31:02,600 --> 00:31:06,370
He's the Director of Logistics
and Distribution at Cheongma Food.

540
00:31:10,010 --> 00:31:11,270
(Oh Tae Seop, Cheongma Food)

541
00:31:11,340 --> 00:31:12,640
But this guy?

542
00:31:13,310 --> 00:31:15,380
He isn't just someone
who made it out of nothing.

543
00:31:15,880 --> 00:31:17,580
He was pretty much...

544
00:31:18,310 --> 00:31:19,750
a nobody.

545
00:31:21,280 --> 00:31:22,750
What do you mean?

546
00:31:35,200 --> 00:31:37,830
All he ever did was drive a truck...

547
00:31:37,900 --> 00:31:39,540
for a Cheongma Logistics
subcontractor.

548
00:31:40,440 --> 00:31:42,240
But after serving time,

549
00:31:42,310 --> 00:31:44,970
he went straight to work
at Cheongma Food.

550
00:31:45,980 --> 00:31:48,680
From there, he shot right up
the corporate ladder...

551
00:31:49,010 --> 00:31:50,980
and snagged the director position.

552
00:31:51,710 --> 00:31:55,820
Man, whether he took a bribe
or offered one,

553
00:31:55,990 --> 00:31:57,420
it's totally suspicious.

554
00:31:58,390 --> 00:31:59,390
I see.

555
00:31:59,990 --> 00:32:01,390
Understood. Good work.

556
00:32:06,500 --> 00:32:09,000
On the day my husband died,

557
00:32:09,700 --> 00:32:12,700
you were shouting at him.

558
00:32:13,640 --> 00:32:15,310
You yelled at him,
saying he just needed...

559
00:32:15,310 --> 00:32:16,740
to shut his mouth.

560
00:32:16,840 --> 00:32:20,440
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

561
00:32:20,510 --> 00:32:22,350
On the day of the accident,

562
00:32:23,480 --> 00:32:26,420
Kang Young Hoon and Cha Seong Woo
had a massive fight,

563
00:32:27,150 --> 00:32:29,290
and the driver responsible
for the crash...

564
00:32:30,450 --> 00:32:32,490
became a director at Cheongma Food?

565
00:32:35,260 --> 00:32:36,260
Kang Young Hoon.

566
00:32:37,690 --> 00:32:39,200
This is too easy.

567
00:32:41,500 --> 00:32:43,800
- Hello.
- Consistently...

568
00:33:29,650 --> 00:33:33,380
(A Trap Called Desire)

569
00:33:33,680 --> 00:33:35,250
At this extraordinary board meeting,

570
00:33:35,390 --> 00:33:37,120
we'll definitely be able
to settle this.

571
00:33:37,320 --> 00:33:39,720
Is this what you've been
secretly working on?

572
00:33:39,920 --> 00:33:42,190
The more I dig,
the more interesting it gets.

573
00:33:42,390 --> 00:33:44,130
When should I drop this bomb?

574
00:33:44,130 --> 00:33:46,100
Can you also keep me updated...

575
00:33:46,130 --> 00:33:48,970
on So Yeon's health
and her overall situation?

576
00:33:49,130 --> 00:33:51,600
But why did Dad suddenly
change his mind?

577
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:53,900
Eun Seol, could you
take a picture of us?

578
00:33:54,100 --> 00:33:56,110
Digging deeper into Director Joo
is way too dangerous.

579
00:33:56,170 --> 00:33:57,240
If I act rashly,

580
00:33:57,340 --> 00:33:58,510
there's no telling
what she might do.

581
00:33:58,570 --> 00:33:59,580
You remember me, right?

582
00:33:59,640 --> 00:34:01,380
Is the retrial preparation
going well?

583
00:34:01,610 --> 00:34:04,380
Have you turned up anything
on Manager Na?

584
00:34:05,110 --> 00:34:07,120
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
